msgid "1 (Gentle · intervenes past half queue, prioritizes throughput & compatibility)"
msgstr ""

msgid "1. Centrally manage low-level RTL9617C NIC and forwarding ASIC offload features, kept separate from QoS shaping and queueing."
msgstr ""

msgid "1. Click \"Add\" under \"Per-Device Rate Limiting Rules\" below and select your phone, PC, or TV from the \"Device MAC Address\" dropdown."
msgstr ""

msgid "1. Configure scheduling and rate limits on physical Ethernet ports (LAN1–LAN4) and the PON optical port (pon0) using the ASIC's 8-level hardware priority queues."
msgstr ""

msgid "1. During port scans, SYN/ICMP floods, or malformed packet attacks, software firewalls on traditional routers can max out the CPU and drop connectivity. With this master switch enabled, the RTL9617C ASIC inspects and drops all 16 attack types at the physical port front-end with 0% CPU usage."
msgstr ""

msgid "1. Easiest setup: click \"Esports Gaming & Voice Anti-Lag\" or \"Work-From-Home & Video Conferencing Priority\" under \"One-Click Scenario Presets\" below to automatically enable small-packet priority, load the app signature catalog, and configure port hardware queueing."
msgstr ""

msgid "1. Manage the RTL9617C forwarding ASIC's per-flow policer channels (0–159) and multi-flow shared policer groups (0–63) for precise hardware rate limiting and burst control."
msgstr ""

msgid "1. When hardware flowtable offload is enabled, established forwarded packets are switched directly in silicon between ports without reaching the router CPU, so running tcpdump on the router cannot see offloaded traffic."
msgstr ""

msgid "1. With \"L2TPv2 / PPTP Hardware Offload\" enabled, plaintext PPP-encapsulated L2TPv2 (UDP 1701) and PPTP (GREv1) data planes are encapsulated/decapsulated directly by the RTL9617C L3PE dual-header tunnel ASIC, sharply reducing CPU usage."
msgstr ""

msgid "10000 (~10 Mbps)"
msgstr ""

msgid "100000 (~100 Mbps)"
msgstr ""

msgid "1000000 (~1000 Mbps)"
msgstr ""

msgid "128 bytes (tiny control / voice frames only)"
msgstr ""

msgid "15 safe protection rules are enabled by default (excluding syn1024, which blocks 80/443 replies). Select any rule here to disable it individually if false positives occur."
msgstr ""

msgid "16 Attack Protection Rules Status"
msgstr ""

msgid "160 channels total"
msgstr ""

msgid "2 (Balanced · throttles earlier, balances low latency & throughput)"
msgstr ""

msgid "2. \"Host TX Offload (DMA LSO)\" accelerates heavy local router uploads (such as Samba, web server, proxy, or iperf3 server on the router) by offloading checksumming and TCP segmentation to DMA LSO hardware; the status card verifies live ethtool NIC flags."
msgstr ""

msgid "2. Choosing a mode: (a) To cap total download speed on a LAN port, select \"Port Download Shaping\"; (b) To let high-priority gaming/voice traffic always go first, select \"Strict Priority Queueing\" (VoQ 7 highest → VoQ 0 lowest); (c) Recommended: \"Hybrid Priority Queueing (ETS)\", e.g., top 3 high-priority queues (CoS 7–5) strict and CoS 4–0 sharing bandwidth by weight. (Note: pon0 hardware PUC supports sp and ets only.)"
msgstr ""

msgid "2. For per-device rate limiting, use Per-Device Rate Limiting (which has 96 dedicated reserved hardware channels); the 160 channels and 64 shared groups here are for fine-grained flow-level policing."
msgstr ""

msgid "2. If a tunnel negotiates MPPE encryption, CCP compression, VJ compression, or IPsec encapsulation, the kernel safely falls back to software processing without affecting connectivity."
msgstr ""

msgid "2. Recommended setup: check \"Enable Hardware Automatic DoS Blocking\" below and click \"Save & Apply\". Safe default flood thresholds (ICMP 1000 / SYN 2000 / FIN 2000) and zero-CPU hardware drop on physical ports (excluding CPU ports) are configured automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "2. Smart App Signature Detection: %d app signatures loaded (%s), using dnsmasq nftset to dynamically track domain server IPs + dedicated narrow-port matching with zero ongoing CPU overhead and full ASIC hardware acceleration. Click \"Manage Catalog / Batch Import\" below to add, edit, or import rules freely (applies to direct or proxy-bypassed traffic)."
msgstr ""

msgid "2. Speed unit conversion: 1000 kbps ≈ 1 Mbps (e.g. 50000 for 50 Mbps, 100000 for 100 Mbps, 1000000 for 1000 Mbps)."
msgstr ""

msgid "2. To capture packets for troubleshooting, enable \"Hardware Flow Traffic Mirroring\" here: the ASIC mirrors matching offloaded packets in real time to a chosen physical LAN port (LAN1–LAN4), where a connected PC running Wireshark can capture them."
msgstr ""

msgid "20000 (~20 Mbps)"
msgstr ""

msgid "200000 (~200 Mbps)"
msgstr ""

msgid "256 bytes (recommended · covers most gaming & voice packets)"
msgstr ""

msgid "3 (Aggressive Low-Latency · earliest intervention to prevent ping spikes)"
msgstr ""

msgid "3. \"Zero-Copy RX (page_pool)\" eliminates full-packet CPU memcpy on receive to lower CPU usage for non-offloaded flows (proxy/VPN/Wi-Fi bridging); \"Multi-Core RX Steering\" pins NI IRQs and distributes PON & LAN receive across CPU cores with RPS+RFS."
msgstr ""

msgid "3. Advanced customization: you can also add, edit, or delete rules by LAN device IP (e.g. 192.168.2.100), MAC, or specific game ports in the \"Custom Priority Forwarding Rules\" section at the bottom."
msgstr ""

msgid "3. Enabling \"Hardware Queue Anti-Bufferbloat (WRED)\" below is recommended to reduce queueing delay under saturation. (Note: NIC TX offload and IPTV multicast offload switches are in Network → Hardware Offload.)"
msgstr ""

msgid "3. Hardware DoS Protection and Hardware Traffic Mirroring are now separate pages:"
msgstr ""

msgid "3. If false positives occur during speed tests, LAN scanning, or NAT traversal, exempt individual checks under \"Exempted (Disabled) Attack Types\" or raise the flood rate thresholds."
msgstr ""

msgid "3. The router includes l2tp_ppp and pptp kernel modules plus xl2tpd/pppd plugins; once you add and connect an L2TP or PPTP client interface under Network → Interfaces, ASIC slot allocations and flow references appear here automatically."
msgstr ""

msgid "3. To monitor real-time speed and total traffic for a device without throttling it, set both \"Upload Limit\" and \"Download Limit\" to 0 (0 = unlimited, stats only)."
msgstr ""

msgid "3. To prevent loopback storms, mirroring to router CPU ports is blocked by the driver. Disable mirroring after troubleshooting to avoid consuming extra port bandwidth."
msgstr ""

